						}
						else if (_session?.Comparison.Status == "grounding")
						{
							<div class="compare-status working" role="status" aria-live="polite"><span class="working-spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Answers collected. Retrieving the official Google Cloud documentation to judge against<span class="working-dots"><i>.</i><i>.</i><i>.</i></span>@JudgeElapsed</span></div>
						}
						else if (_session?.Comparison.Status == "failed")
						{
							<div class="compare-status failed" role="alert">@(_session?.Comparison.Error ?? "The comparison did not complete.")</div>
						}

						@if (_session?.Comparison.Sources.Count > 0)
						{
							<section class="rt-box">
								<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">D</span><div><strong>Documentation actually retrieved</strong><small>@_session.Comparison.Sources.Count(source => source.Retrieved) of @_session.Comparison.Sources.Count fetched · @_session.Comparison.GroundingTokens.ToString("N0") tokens in the judge prompt</small></div></header>
								<table class="audit-table">
									<thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Page</th><th>Characters used</th><th>Retrieved at</th></tr></thead>
									<tbody>
										@foreach (var source in _session.Comparison.Sources)
										{
											<tr class="@(source.Retrieved ? "p0-opt" : "p0-req")">
												<td>@(source.Retrieved ? (source.FromCache ? "cached" : "fetched") : "FAILED")</td>
												<td><a href="@source.Url" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@source.Title</a><br /><code>@source.Url</code></td>
												<td>@(source.Retrieved ? source.Characters.ToString("N0") + (source.Truncated ? " (truncated)" : "") : "—")</td>
												<td>@(source.Retrieved ? source.AttemptedAt.ToLocalTime().ToString("HH:mm:ss") : source.Error)</td>
											</tr>
										}
									</tbody>
								</table>
								<p class="ctx-method">This is the text the judge read. Nothing else was supplied to it about Google Cloud, and the three candidate models never saw any of it.</p>
							</section>
						}

						@if (_session?.Comparison.Verdict is { } verdict)
						{
							<aside class="compare-verdict">
								<p class="eyebrow">GROUNDED JUDGE VERDICT</p>
								<div class="coach-label">Scored by @verdict.JudgeModel against documentation retrieved at judging time — blinded and rubric-based, still not a validated benchmark.</div>
								@if (verdict.Ranking.Count > 0)
								{
									<ol class="verdict-ranking">
										@foreach (var slot in verdict.Ranking)
										{
											<li><span class="slot-badge">@slot</span> @ModelForSlot(slot)</li>
										}
									</ol>
								}
								<p class="verdict-rationale">@verdict.Rationale</p>

								@foreach (var score in verdict.Scores.Where(item => item.Evidence.Count > 0 || item.Unsupported.Count > 0))
								{
									<h4>Answer @score.Slot — @ModelForSlot(score.Slot)</h4>
									@if (score.Evidence.Count > 0)
									{
										<p class="eyebrow">DOCUMENTATION QUOTED IN SUPPORT</p>
										<ul class="rt-list good">@foreach (var quote in score.Evidence) { <li>@quote</li> }</ul>
									}
									@if (score.Unsupported.Count > 0)
									{
										<p class="eyebrow">NOT COVERED BY THE RETRIEVED DOCS — NEITHER CONFIRMED NOR REFUTED</p>
										<ul class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var claim in score.Unsupported) { <li>@claim</li> }</ul>
									}
								}

								@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(verdict.CoverageNote))
								{
									<h4>Limits of this evidence</h4>
									<p class="verdict-caveat">@verdict.CoverageNote</p>
								}
								<dl class="verdict-meta"><dt>Judge</dt><dd>@verdict.JudgeModel</dd></dl>
								@if (JudgeSharesCandidateModel)
								{
									<p class="verdict-caveat">Caveat: the judge resolved to the same underlying model as a candidate in this environment. Independence is reduced — treat the ranking with extra caution.</p>
								}
								@if (DuplicateModels)
								{
									<p class="verdict-caveat">Note: two or more columns resolved to the same underlying model. Sign in to additional model families in VS Code for a meaningful comparison.</p>
								}
								<p class="verdict-caveat">Keyword coverage beside each answer is a separate deterministic measure. It counts vocabulary, not correctness — a wrong answer using the right words still scores well on it, which is why the judge's grounded factuality score sits alongside it rather than being replaced by it.</p>
							</aside>
						}
					</section>
					break;
				case 9:
					<section>
						<p class="kicker">ONE MODEL GROUNDS ANOTHER</p>
						<h2 id="scene-title">Using a specialist model as a source, not an oracle</h2>
						<p class="rt-intro">Claude's knowledge of Google Cloud has a boundary; a Google-specialist model may sit past it. The legitimate pattern is to treat the specialist as a <strong>retrieval and gap-finding instrument</strong> — harvest its services, constraints and citations — then have the designer state plainly what it already knew, what it just learned, and what it refuses to trust until the primary docs are checked. Model output is a claim with provenance, never a baseline of truth.</p>

						<section class="rt-box rt-input-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">1</span><div><strong>Design requirement — migrate to GCP</strong><small>editable</small></div></header>
							<textarea class="rt-code-input" spellcheck="false" maxlength="8000" @bind="_supportRequirement" @bind:event="oninput" disabled="@SupportBusy" aria-label="GCP migration requirement"></textarea>
							<div class="rt-actions">
								<small>@_supportRequirement.Length / 8000</small>
								<button class="primary-command compact" type="button" data-auto="s11.run" disabled="@(!_bridgeConnected || _supportRequirement.Trim().Length < 20 || SupportBusy)" @onclick="RunLlmSupport">@SupportButtonText</button>
							</div>
							@if (!_bridgeConnected)
							{
								<p class="bridge-required" role="status">Connect the VSIX with the token shown under Local Bridge before running.</p>
							}
						</section>

						<section class="rt-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">2</span><div><strong>Gemini's role &amp; answer</strong><small>@(_session?.LlmSupport.AdviceModel ?? "Gemini 3.7 Flash") · retrieval instrument, not the designer</small></div></header>
							@if (_session?.LlmSupport.Advice is { } geminiAdvice)
							{
								<div class="audit-body">
									<div class="compare-status" role="status">Role: surface GCP-specific services, constraints, and authoritative citations. Its output is an <strong>unverified model claim</strong> passed downstream as evidence, not as truth.</div>
									<p class="rt-reco">@geminiAdvice.Overview</p>
									@if (geminiAdvice.Services.Count > 0)
									{
										<h4>Services surfaced</h4><ul class="mod-service-list">@foreach (var service in geminiAdvice.Services) { <li>@service</li> }</ul>
									}
									@if (geminiAdvice.Constraints.Count > 0)
									{
										<h4>Platform constraints</h4><ul class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var constraint in geminiAdvice.Constraints) { <li>@constraint</li> }</ul>
									}
									@if (geminiAdvice.Citations.Count > 0)
									{
										<h4>Cited documentation (the part worth keeping)</h4><ul class="rt-list good">@foreach (var citation in geminiAdvice.Citations) { <li><code>@citation</code></li> }</ul>
									}
								</div>
							}
							else if (_session?.LlmSupport.Status == "advising")
							{
								<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Gemini is surfacing GCP services, constraints and citations…</div>
							}
							else
							{
								<div class="rt-placeholder">Gemini's surfaced services, constraints and documentation links will appear here.</div>
							}
						</section>

						<section class="rt-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">3</span><div><strong>Claude's use of that information</strong><small>the knowledge boundary, stated honestly</small></div></header>
							@if (_session?.LlmSupport.Synthesis is { } synth)
							{
								<div class="audit-body">
									<div class="know-grid">
										<div class="know-col own">
											<p class="eyebrow">ALREADY KNEW</p>
											<ul>@foreach (var item in synth.AlreadyKnew) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
										</div>
										<div class="know-col learned">
											<p class="eyebrow">LEARNED FROM GEMINI</p>
											<ul>@foreach (var item in synth.LearnedFromGemini) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
										</div>
										<div class="know-col unverified">
											<p class="eyebrow">WILL NOT TRUST UNVERIFIED</p>
											<ul>@foreach (var item in synth.NeedsVerification) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
										</div>
									</div>
								</div>
							}
							else if (_session?.LlmSupport.Status is "advising" or "synthesizing")
							{
								<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Claude is separating what it knew from what it learned…</div>
							}
							else
							{
								<div class="rt-placeholder">Claude's knowledge-boundary breakdown will appear here.</div>
							}
						</section>

						<section class="rt-qa">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">4</span><div><strong>Final design implementation</strong><small>every step tagged with its source</small></div></header>
							@if (_session?.LlmSupport.Synthesis is { } design)
							{
								<div class="coach-label">Designed by @_session.LlmSupport.SynthesisModel using @(_session.LlmSupport.AdviceModel ?? "the advisory") as a cited source — not as a baseline.</div>
								<p class="rt-reco">@design.DesignSummary</p>
								<table class="audit-table">
									<thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Detail</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
									<tbody>
										@foreach (var step in design.DesignSteps)
										{
											<tr>
												<td>@step.Step</td>
												<td>@step.Detail</td>
												<td><span class="src-tag src-@step.Source">@(step.Source switch { "own" => "Claude", "gemini" => "Gemini + verified", _ => "needs verification" })</span></td>
											</tr>
										}
									</tbody>
								</table>
								@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(design.ProvenanceNote))
								{
									<h4>Before this design is trusted</h4><p class="rt-reco">@design.ProvenanceNote</p>
								}
							}
							else if (_session?.LlmSupport.Status == "synthesizing")
							{
								<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Claude is producing the grounded migration design…</div>
							}
							else
							{
								<div class="rt-placeholder">The final, source-tagged migration design will appear here.</div>
							}
							@if (_session?.LlmSupport.Status == "failed")
							{
								<div class="compare-status failed" role="alert">@(_session?.LlmSupport.Error ?? "The demo did not complete.")</div>
							}
						</section>
					</section>
					break;
				case 10:
					<section>
						<p class="kicker">GROUNDING ROUND TRIP</p>
						<h2 id="scene-title">Class ? JIRA story ? class</h2>
						<p class="rt-intro">Gemma 4 reads a class and writes the JIRA story it satisfies, then rebuilds the class from <em>only that story</em>. Claude Opus 5.0 then reviews how much of the original behavior survived the round trip. This measures how well a generated artifact grounds a faithful reconstruction — it is coaching commentary, not a validated grade.</p>

						<section class="rt-box rt-input-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">1</span><div><strong>Original class</strong><small>input to Gemma 4</small></div></header>
							<textarea class="rt-code-input" spellcheck="false" maxlength="12000" @bind="_roundTripClass" @bind:event="oninput" disabled="@RoundTripBusy" aria-label="Original class"></textarea>
							<div class="rt-actions">
								<small>@_roundTripClass.Length / 12000</small>
								<button class="primary-command compact" type="button" data-auto="s12.run" disabled="@(!_bridgeConnected || _roundTripClass.Trim().Length < 20 || RoundTripBusy)" @onclick="RunRoundTrip">@RoundTripButtonText</button>
							</div>
							@if (!_bridgeConnected)
							{
								<p class="bridge-required" role="status">Connect the VSIX with the token shown under Local Bridge before running the round trip.</p>
							}
						</section>

						<div class="rt-flow rt-flow-stacked">
							<section class="rt-box">
								<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">2</span><div><strong>JIRA story</strong><small>@(_session?.RoundTrip.StoryModel ?? "Gemma 4")@(_session?.RoundTrip.StoryFallbackUsed == true ? " · substitute" : string.Empty)</small></div></header>
								@if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_session?.RoundTrip.Story))
								{
									<div class="rt-story">@_session.RoundTrip.Story</div>
								}
								else if (_session?.RoundTrip.Status is "queued" or "story")
								{
									<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Gemma is drafting the JIRA story…</div>
								}
								else
								{
									<div class="rt-placeholder">The generated JIRA story will appear here.</div>
								}
							</section>

							<section class="rt-box">
								<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">3</span><div><strong>Re-created class</strong><small>@(_session?.RoundTrip.RecreatedModel ?? "Gemma 4")@(_session?.RoundTrip.RecreatedFallbackUsed == true ? " · substitute" : string.Empty) · from story only</small></div></header>
								@if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_session?.RoundTrip.RecreatedClass))
								{
									<pre class="rt-code">@_session.RoundTrip.RecreatedClass</pre>
								}
								else if (_session?.RoundTrip.Status == "recreating")
								{
									<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Gemma is rebuilding the class from the story…</div>
								}
								else
								{
									<div class="rt-placeholder">The reconstructed class will appear here.</div>
								}
							</section>
						</div>

						@if (_session?.RoundTrip.Status == "failed")
						{
							<div class="compare-status failed" role="alert">@(_session?.RoundTrip.Error ?? "The round trip did not complete.")</div>
						}

						<section class="rt-qa">
							<p class="eyebrow">QA — ORIGINAL vs RE-CREATED</p>
							@if (_session?.RoundTrip.Qa is { } qa)
							{
								<div class="coach-label">Claude QA — behavioral fidelity review, not a validated grade.</div>
								<div class="rt-fidelity"><span class="rt-score">@qa.Fidelity<small>/5</small></span><div><strong>Behavioral fidelity</strong><p>@qa.Summary</p></div></div>
								@if (qa.Preserved.Count > 0)
								{
									<h4>Preserved behavior</h4><ul class="rt-list good">@foreach (var item in qa.Preserved) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
								}
								@if (qa.Gaps.Count > 0)
								{
									<h4>Lost or changed</h4><ul class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var item in qa.Gaps) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
								}
								@if (qa.Risks.Count > 0)
								{
									<h4>Risks</h4><ul class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var item in qa.Risks) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
								}
								@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(qa.Recommendation))
								{
									<h4>Recommendation</h4><p class="rt-reco">@qa.Recommendation</p>
								}
								<small>Reviewed by @_session.RoundTrip.QaModel</small>
							}
							else if (_session?.RoundTrip.Status == "qa")
							{
								<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Claude is comparing the original and re-created classes…</div>
							}
							else
							{
								<div class="rt-placeholder">Claude's fidelity review of the original versus the re-created class will appear here.</div>
							}
						</section>
					</section>
					break;
				case 11:
					<section>
						<p class="kicker">MODERNIZE FOR AI-FRIENDLINESS</p>
						<h2 id="scene-title">Spend comprehension tokens once</h2>
						<p class="rt-intro">Old procedural code is a recurring token tax — every fix and every agent run re-derives its intent. Modernize it once: Claude Opus 5.0 refactors the code behavior-preservingly, then explains it and exposes the business rules so it can be tested and split into microservices. Teaching illustration, not a validated migration.</p>

						<section class="rt-box rt-input-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">1</span><div><strong>Legacy code</strong><small>procedural · hard to read</small></div></header>
							<textarea class="rt-code-input" spellcheck="false" maxlength="12000" @bind="_legacyCode" @bind:event="oninput" disabled="@ModernizeBusy" aria-label="Legacy code"></textarea>
							<div class="rt-actions">
								<small>@_legacyCode.Length / 12000</small>
								<button class="primary-command compact" type="button" data-auto="s13.run" disabled="@(!_bridgeConnected || _legacyCode.Trim().Length < 20 || ModernizeBusy)" @onclick="RunModernize">@ModernizeButtonText</button>
							</div>
							@if (!_bridgeConnected)
							{
								<p class="bridge-required" role="status">Connect the VSIX with the token shown under Local Bridge before modernizing.</p>
							}
						</section>

						<section class="rt-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">2</span><div><strong>Modernized code</strong><small>@(_session?.Modernize.Model ?? "Claude Opus 5.0") · behavior-preserving</small></div></header>
							@if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_session?.Modernize.Result?.ModernizedCode))
							{
								<pre class="rt-code">@_session.Modernize.Result.ModernizedCode</pre>
							}
							else if (ModernizeBusy)
							{
								<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Claude is modernizing the code…</div>
							}
							else
							{
								<div class="rt-placeholder">The refactored, modernized code will appear here.</div>
							}
						</section>

						@if (_session?.Modernize.Status == "failed")
						{
							<div class="compare-status failed" role="alert">@(_session?.Modernize.Error ?? "The modernization did not complete.")</div>
						}

						<section class="rt-qa">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">3</span><div><strong>Explanation &amp; exposed business logic</strong><small>where a service boundary could be drawn</small></div></header>
							@if (_session?.Modernize.Result is { } modern)
							{
								<div class="coach-label">AI explanation — verify against characterization tests and the SME before any migration.</div>
								<p class="rt-reco">@modern.Explanation</p>
								@if (modern.BusinessRules.Count > 0)
								{
									<h4>Business rules exposed</h4><ul class="rt-list good">@foreach (var rule in modern.BusinessRules) { <li>@rule</li> }</ul>
								}
								@if (modern.MicroserviceCandidates.Count > 0)
								{
									<h4>Microservice candidates</h4><ul class="mod-service-list">@foreach (var candidate in modern.MicroserviceCandidates) { <li>@candidate</li> }</ul>
								}
								<small>Modernized by @_session.Modernize.Model</small>
							}
							else if (ModernizeBusy)
							{
								<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Waiting for the modernization to finish…</div>
							}
							else
							{
								<div class="rt-placeholder">A plain-language explanation, the exposed business rules, and candidate microservice boundaries will appear here.</div>
							}
						</section>
					</section>
					break;
				case 12:
					<section>
						<p class="kicker">AGENTIC-READINESS AUDIT · CODE</p>
						<h2 id="scene-title">Rate the code deterministically, then let Gemma advise</h2>
						<p class="rt-intro">Auditing hundreds of repos needs a reproducible signal first. Roslyn parses the C# into a syntax graph and computes a deterministic agentic-readiness rating; Gemma 4 then grounds its recommendations on that rating. The numbers come from static analysis and never change — the model only supplies judgment. (Java repos use Spoon / JavaParser through the same metric schema.)</p>

						<section class="rt-box rt-input-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">1</span><div><strong>Sample C# project</strong><small>static analysis only · code is never executed</small></div></header>
							<textarea class="rt-code-input" spellcheck="false" maxlength="16000" @bind="_auditCode" @bind:event="oninput" disabled="@AuditBusy" aria-label="C# project to audit"></textarea>
							<div class="rt-actions">
								<small>@_auditCode.Length / 16000</small>
								<button class="primary-command compact" type="button" data-auto="s14.run" disabled="@(!_bridgeConnected || _auditCode.Trim().Length < 20 || AuditBusy)" @onclick="RunAudit">@AuditButtonText</button>
							</div>
							@if (!_bridgeConnected)
							{
								<p class="bridge-required" role="status">Connect the VSIX with the token shown under Local Bridge before auditing.</p>
							}
						</section>

						<section class="rt-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">2</span><div><strong>Roslyn analysis</strong><small>deterministic · reproducible</small></div></header>
							@if (_session?.Audit.Report is { ParseError: false } report)
							{
								<div class="audit-body">
									<div class="audit-scoreline">
										<span class="audit-grade grade-@report.Grade.ToLowerInvariant()">@report.Grade</span>
										<div><strong>@report.OverallScore/100</strong><small>agentic-readiness</small></div>
										<p>@report.Summary</p>
									</div>
									<div class="audit-dims">
										@foreach (var dim in report.Dimensions)
										{
											<div class="audit-dim">
												<div class="audit-dim-head"><span>@dim.Dimension</span><b>@dim.Value</b></div>
												<div class="audit-bar"><i style="width:@dim.Value%"></i></div>
												<small>@dim.Detail</small>
											</div>
										}
									</div>
									<h4>Findings</h4>
									<ul class="audit-findings">
										@foreach (var finding in report.Findings)
										{
											<li><span class="sev @SeverityClass(finding.Severity)">@finding.Severity</span>@finding.Message</li>
										}
									</ul>
									<h4>Types</h4>
									<table class="audit-table">
										<thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Methods</th><th>Public</th><th>Lines</th><th>Depends on</th></tr></thead>
										<tbody>
											@foreach (var type in report.Types)
											{
												<tr><td>@type.Kind @type.Name</td><td>@type.Methods</td><td>@type.PublicMembers</td><td>@type.Lines</td><td>@(type.DependsOn.Count > 0 ? string.Join(", ", type.DependsOn) : "—")</td></tr>
											}
										</tbody>
									</table>
									<h4>Type dependency graph</h4>
									<div class="audit-graph">@(report.GraphEdges.Count > 0 ? string.Join("  ·  ", report.GraphEdges) : "No internal type dependencies.")</div>
								</div>
							}
							else if (_session?.Audit.Status == "failed" && _session?.Audit.Report is { ParseError: true })
							{
								<div class="compare-status failed" role="alert">@(_session?.Audit.Error ?? "The code could not be analyzed.")</div>
							}
							else
							{
								<div class="rt-placeholder">The deterministic Roslyn rating, metrics, findings, and dependency graph will appear here.</div>
							}
						</section>

						<section class="rt-qa">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">3</span><div><strong>Gemma 4 audit feedback</strong><small>grounded on the Roslyn rating</small></div></header>
							@if (_session?.Audit.Recommendation is { } advice)
							{
								<div class="coach-label">AI recommendations grounded on the deterministic rating — the scores above are authoritative.</div>
								<p class="rt-reco">@advice.Summary</p>
								@if (advice.Strengths.Count > 0)
								{
									<h4>Strengths</h4><ul class="rt-list good">@foreach (var item in advice.Strengths) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
								}
								@if (advice.Priorities.Count > 0)
								{
									<h4>Priority fixes</h4><ol class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var item in advice.Priorities) { <li>@item</li> }</ol>
								}
								@if (advice.AgenticReadiness.Count > 0)
								{
									<h4>To become agentic-ready</h4><ul class="rt-list good">@foreach (var item in advice.AgenticReadiness) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
								}
								<small>Reviewed by @_session.Audit.Model</small>
							}
							else if (_session?.Audit.Status is "analyzed" or "queued" or "running")
							{
								<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Gemma is drafting recommendations from the deterministic rating…</div>
							}
							else if (_session?.Audit.Status == "failed" && _session?.Audit.Report is { ParseError: false })
							{
								<div class="compare-status failed" role="alert">@(_session?.Audit.Error ?? "The audit review did not complete.")</div>
							}
							else
							{
								<div class="rt-placeholder">Gemma's grounded recommendations will appear here after analysis.</div>
							}
						</section>
					</section>
					break;
				case 13:
					<section>
						<p class="kicker">AGENTIC-READINESS AUDIT · CONTEXT</p>
						<h2 id="scene-title">Does the context actually help an agent?</h2>
						<p class="rt-intro">A three-tier funnel for thousands of repos: a deterministic scan finds context structures (OKF, memory-bank, wiki, ADRs), an ML.NET classifier (embeddinggemma-300m embeddings in production) predicts readiness cheaply, and only if that passes does Gemma 4 run the deep audit. Its context is then tested against 5 planted traps, and Claude Opus 5.0 grades how many Gemma caught.</p>

