						}
					</section>
					break;
				case 25:
					<section>
						<p class="kicker">GREEN TESTS ARE NOT COVERAGE</p>
						<h2 id="scene-title">Does the suite cover the risk this change adds?</h2>
						<p class="rt-intro">Three questions, three different techniques. <strong>Does the candidate still agree with production?</strong> Only executing both against real condition data can answer that. <strong>Does the data reach the whole logic space?</strong> Static analysis finds the branches; execution proves which ones fired. <strong>Would a test notice if a line were wrong?</strong> That is mutation testing. Passing any one of the three proves nothing about the other two.</p>

						<section class="rt-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">?</span><div><strong>What Roslyn can and cannot tell you</strong><small>the limit that makes the rest of this tab necessary</small></div></header>
							<div class="audit-body">
								<p class="rt-reco"><strong>Roslyn is a static analyser. It does not run the code.</strong> It parses source into a syntax tree and can tell you, with certainty, what the code <em>says</em>. It cannot tell you what the code <em>does</em> with your data.</p>
								<table class="audit-table">
									<thead><tr><th>Roslyn answers this</th><th>Roslyn cannot answer this</th></tr></thead>
									<tbody>
										<tr><td>Which branch predicates exist, and on which lines</td><td>Which of those branches your test data actually reaches</td></tr>
										<tr><td>Where the operators and literals are, so defects can be injected</td><td>Whether the enhanced service still agrees with production</td></tr>
										<tr><td>That a method is unreachable or a variable unused</td><td>Whether a passing test asserted anything meaningful</td></tr>
										<tr><td>Structural shape of the change</td><td>Whether a behaviour difference was requested or is a regression</td></tr>
									</tbody>
								</table>
								<p class="rt-reco">So this tab uses Roslyn for exactly what it is good at &mdash; <strong>finding the predicates and the mutation sites</strong> &mdash; and then <strong>executes</strong> code to answer everything else.</p>
								<h4>Why a production baseline is the reference</h4>
								<p>Consider a service taking <code>A</code>, <code>B</code>, <code>C</code> with logic <code>if (A &gt; 0)</code>, <code>if (B &lt; 2)</code>, <code>if (C == 0)</code>. Reading that tells you three predicates exist. It does not tell you what the service returns for <code>0, 1, 4</code>. The only trustworthy answer to <em>"did we break anything?"</em> is the behaviour of the version already running in production &mdash; the <strong>golden baseline</strong> &mdash; run against the same inputs.</p>
								<div class="pipeline-chain">
									<span>production baseline</span><span>QA candidate</span><span>same condition data</span><span>compare responses</span><span>classify each difference</span>
								</div>
								<p class="rt-reco">A difference is not automatically a defect. If the business asked for it, the team records it as a <strong>signed-off change</strong> and writes a new functional test &mdash; which then joins the regression suite permanently. A difference matching no signed-off rule is a <strong>regression</strong> until someone says otherwise.</p>
								<h4>What this tab does not measure</h4>
								<pre class="rt-code">@RegressionSamples.FaultInjectionNote</pre>
								<p class="ctx-method">Recorded so nobody mistakes condition-permutation agreement for complete regression assurance. Fault injection is a separate discipline and is not executed here.</p>
							</div>
						</section>

						<section class="rt-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">1</span><div><strong>Production baseline</strong><small>the golden reference &middot; what runs today</small></div></header>
							<textarea class="rt-code-input tall" spellcheck="false" maxlength="8000" @bind="_regressionBaseline" @bind:event="oninput" disabled="@_mutationRunning" aria-label="Baseline"></textarea>
						</section>

						<section class="rt-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">2</span><div><strong>The enhancement</strong><small>what the business asked for</small></div></header>
							<div class="audit-body">
								<pre class="rt-code">@RegressionSamples.Enhancement</pre>
								<h4>Signed-off behaviour changes</h4>
								<table class="audit-table">
									<thead><tr><th>Applies when</th><th>Authority</th></tr></thead>
									<tbody>
										@foreach (var signedOff in RegressionSamples.IntendedChanges)
										{
											<tr><td><code>@signedOff.Rule</code></td><td>@signedOff.Description</td></tr>
										}
									</tbody>
								</table>
								<p class="ctx-method">These are the only differences the comparison will accept without escalation.</p>
							</div>
						</section>

						<section class="rt-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">3</span><div><strong>Enhanced candidate</strong><small>the QA build &middot; editable</small></div></header>
							<textarea class="rt-code-input tall" spellcheck="false" maxlength="8000" @bind="_regressionSource" @bind:event="oninput" disabled="@_mutationRunning" aria-label="Source"></textarea>
						</section>

						<section class="rt-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">4</span><div><strong>Existing test suite</strong><small>currently passing</small></div></header>
							<textarea class="rt-code-input tall" spellcheck="false" maxlength="8000" @bind="_regressionTests" @bind:event="oninput" disabled="@_mutationRunning" aria-label="Tests"></textarea>
						</section>

						<section class="rt-box" data-auto="s26.vectors">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">5</span><div><strong>QA condition data</strong><small>one row per permutation &middot; columns bind to the parameters in order</small></div></header>
							<textarea class="rt-code-input" spellcheck="false" maxlength="4000" @bind="_regressionVectors" @bind:event="oninput" disabled="@_mutationRunning" aria-label="Test vectors"></textarea>
							<div class="audit-body"><p class="ctx-method">This is the artefact QA maintains: every combination of conditions the business logic distinguishes, including the boundaries. Coverage of the logic space is a property of this file, not of the code.</p></div>
						</section>

						<div class="rt-actions">
							<small>Deterministic &mdash; compiles and executes both versions in-process, no model call.</small>
							<button class="primary-command compact" type="button" data-auto="s26.mutate" disabled="@_mutationRunning" @onclick="RunMutation">@(_mutationRunning ? "Running…" : "Run mutation and compare test")</button>
						</div>

						@if (_audit is { } regressionAudit)
						{
							<span data-auto="s26.audit-result" hidden></span>
							<section class="rt-box">
								<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">6</span><div><strong>Comparison against production</strong><small>every row executed through both versions</small></div></header>
								<div class="audit-body">
									@if (!regressionAudit.Differential.Ran)
									{
										<div class="compare-status failed" role="alert">@regressionAudit.Differential.Error</div>
									}
									else
									{
										<div class="audit-scoreline">
											<span class="ctx-label @(regressionAudit.Differential.Unintended > 0 ? "ctx-poor" : regressionAudit.Differential.NotImplemented > 0 ? "ctx-adequate" : "ctx-rich")">@regressionAudit.Differential.Unintended</span>
											<div><strong>Unexplained differences</strong><small>@regressionAudit.Differential.VectorCount rows &middot; @regressionAudit.Differential.Identical identical &middot; @regressionAudit.Differential.Intended intended &middot; @regressionAudit.Differential.NotImplemented to adjudicate</small></div>
											<p>@regressionAudit.Differential.Verdict</p>
										</div>
										<table class="audit-table">
											<thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Inputs</th><th>Production</th><th>Candidate</th><th>Classification</th><th>Basis</th></tr></thead>
											<tbody>
												@foreach (var row in regressionAudit.Differential.Comparisons)
												{
													<tr class="@(row.Classification switch { "REGRESSION" => "p0-req", "adjudicate" => "p0-req", "intended" => "p0-opt", _ => null })">
														<td>@row.Row</td>
														<td><code>@row.Inputs</code></td>
														<td><code>@row.BaselineResult</code></td>
														<td><code>@row.CandidateResult</code></td>
														<td><strong>@row.Classification</strong></td>
														<td>@row.Note</td>
													</tr>
												}
											</tbody>
										</table>
										<p class="ctx-method">Every row classified <em>intended</em> should already have a functional test naming it. If it does not, that test is the deliverable &mdash; and it becomes part of the regression suite from then on.</p>
									}
								</div>
							</section>

							<section class="rt-box">
								<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">7</span><div><strong>Condition coverage of the data</strong><small>Roslyn finds the predicates &middot; execution proves which fired</small></div></header>
								<div class="audit-body">
									@if (!regressionAudit.Coverage.Ran)
									{
										<div class="compare-status failed" role="alert">@regressionAudit.Coverage.Error</div>
									}
									else
									{
										<div class="audit-scoreline">
											<span class="ctx-label @(regressionAudit.Coverage.CoveragePercent >= 100 ? "ctx-rich" : regressionAudit.Coverage.CoveragePercent >= 50 ? "ctx-adequate" : "ctx-poor")">@regressionAudit.Coverage.CoveragePercent%</span>
											<div><strong>Predicates driven both ways</strong><small>@regressionAudit.Coverage.FullyExercised of @regressionAudit.Coverage.Predicates@(regressionAudit.Coverage.SkippedPredicates > 0 ? $" · {regressionAudit.Coverage.SkippedPredicates} not evaluable in isolation" : string.Empty)</small></div>
											<p>@regressionAudit.Coverage.Verdict</p>
										</div>
										<table class="audit-table">
											<thead><tr><th>Line</th><th>Condition</th><th>Driven true</th><th>Driven false</th></tr></thead>
											<tbody>
												@foreach (var predicate in regressionAudit.Coverage.Details)
												{
													<tr class="@(predicate.Evaluable && predicate.TrueSeen && predicate.FalseSeen ? "p0-opt" : "p0-req")">
														<td>@predicate.Line</td>
														<td><code>@predicate.Expression</code></td>
														<td>@(!predicate.Evaluable ? "not evaluable" : predicate.TrueSeen ? "yes" : "NEVER")</td>
														<td>@(!predicate.Evaluable ? "not evaluable" : predicate.FalseSeen ? "yes" : "NEVER")</td>
													</tr>
												}
											</tbody>
										</table>
										<p class="ctx-method">A predicate driven only one way means the QA data never takes the other branch. That is a gap in the <em>data</em>, and no amount of extra assertions on existing rows will close it.</p>
									}
								</div>
							</section>
						}

						@if (_mutation is { } mutation)
						{
							<span data-auto="s26.mutation-result" hidden></span>
							@if (!mutation.Ran)
							{
								<div class="compare-status failed" role="alert">@mutation.Error</div>
							}
							else
							{
								<section class="rt-box">
									<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">8</span><div><strong>Mutation score</strong><small>@mutation.KilledMutants of @mutation.TotalMutants defects caught</small></div></header>
									<div class="audit-body">
										<p class="rt-reco">A different question from the comparison above. Comparison asks <em>"does the candidate still agree with production?"</em>. Mutation asks <strong>"would a test have noticed if this line were wrong?"</strong> — you breed small variants of the working program and count how many the suite detects. <strong>Score = killed ÷ viable mutants.</strong> 100% would mean the suite noticed every defect <em>this tool knows how to inject</em>, not that the code is correct.</p>
										<div class="pipeline-chain">
											<span>compile</span><span>run baseline</span><span>inject one defect</span><span>re-run tests</span><span>killed or survived</span><span>score</span>
										</div>
										<ul class="rt-list warn">
											<li><strong>The baseline suite must be green first.</strong> If it already fails, every mutant looks killed and the score is meaningless. This refuses to run in that state.</li>
											<li><strong>Mutants that will not compile are excluded, not counted as kills.</strong> No test could ever have caught them, so counting them would inflate the score for free.</li>
											<li><strong>Some survivors may be equivalent programs.</strong> The tool cannot detect equivalence, so a survivor is a candidate gap, not a proven one.</li>
										</ul>
									</div>
									<div class="audit-scoreline">
										<span class="ctx-label @(mutation.MutationScore >= 80 ? "ctx-rich" : mutation.MutationScore >= 50 ? "ctx-adequate" : "ctx-poor")">@mutation.MutationScore%</span>
										<div><strong>Mutation score</strong><small>baseline suite: @string.Join(", ", mutation.BaselineTests)</small></div>
										<p>@mutation.Verdict</p>
									</div>
									<table class="audit-table">
										<thead><tr><th>Line</th><th>Injected defect</th><th>Change</th><th>Outcome</th></tr></thead>
										<tbody>
											@foreach (var mutant in mutation.Mutants)
											{
												<tr class="@(mutant.Killed ? "p0-opt" : "p0-req")">
													<td>@mutant.Line</td>
													<td>@mutant.Description</td>
													<td><code>@mutant.Original</code> → <code>@mutant.Mutated</code></td>
													<td>@(mutant.Killed ? $"caught by {mutant.Detail}" : "SURVIVED — no test failed")</td>
												</tr>
											}
										</tbody>
									</table>
									<p class="ctx-method">Every surviving row is a real behaviour change the suite accepted. Add a test until the rows that matter go away.</p>
								</section>

								<section class="rt-box">
									<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">9</span><div><strong>Gemma 4 proposes the missing tests</strong><small>closing named survivors, not "more coverage"</small></div></header>
									<div class="audit-body">
										<p class="rt-reco">A surviving mutant is a <strong>falsifiable target</strong>: either a proposed test fails against the mutated code or it does not. That is why the model is asked to close specific survivors rather than to improve the suite in general — the instruction can be checked.</p>
										<div class="rt-actions">
											<small>Gemma sees the mutation report, the code and the existing tests.</small>
											<button class="primary-command compact" type="button" data-auto="s26.guidance" disabled="@(!_bridgeConnected || GuidanceBusy || mutation.Mutants.All(item => item.Killed))" @onclick="RunRegressionGuidance">@GuidanceButtonText</button>
										</div>
										@if (mutation.Mutants.All(item => item.Killed))
										{
											<p class="ctx-method">Nothing survived, so there is nothing to remediate.</p>
										}
										else if (!_bridgeConnected)
										{
											<p class="bridge-required" role="status">Connect the VSIX with the token shown under Local Bridge before running.</p>
										}
										@if (_session?.RegressionGuidance.Error is { } guidanceError)
										{
											<div class="compare-status failed" role="alert">@guidanceError</div>
										}
										@if (_session?.RegressionGuidance.Remediation is { } remediation)
										{
											<div class="coach-label">Proposed by @remediation.Model</div>
											<p class="rt-reco">@remediation.Summary</p>
											<table class="audit-table">
												<thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>Kills</th><th>Scenario</th><th>Assertion</th></tr></thead>
												<tbody>
													@foreach (var proposal in remediation.Tests)
													{
														<tr><td><code>@proposal.Name</code></td><td>@proposal.TargetsSurvivor</td><td>@proposal.Behaviour</td><td>@proposal.Assertion</td></tr>
													}
												</tbody>
											</table>
											@if (remediation.NotWorthTesting.Count > 0)
											{
												<h4>Deliberately not tested</h4>
												<ul class="rt-list">@foreach (var item in remediation.NotWorthTesting) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
											}
										}
										else if (_session?.RegressionGuidance.Status == "advising")
										{
											<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Gemma is working out which tests would close the survivors…</div>
										}
									</div>
								</section>

								<section class="rt-qa">
									<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">10</span><div><strong>Claude Opus 4.8 checks the proposals</strong><small>would each test actually kill what it claims?</small></div></header>
									@if (_session?.RegressionGuidance.Review is { } guidanceReview)
									{
										<div class="coach-label">Reviewed by @guidanceReview.Model</div>
										<p class="rt-reco">@guidanceReview.Verdict</p>
										<table class="audit-table">
											<thead><tr><th>Proposed test</th><th>Would it kill the mutant?</th><th>Reasoning traced against the code</th></tr></thead>
											<tbody>
												@foreach (var testCheck in guidanceReview.Assessments)
												{
													<tr class="@(testCheck.WouldKill ? "p0-opt" : "p0-req")">
														<td><code>@testCheck.Name</code></td>
														<td>@(testCheck.WouldKill ? "yes" : "NO")</td>
														<td>@testCheck.Reasoning</td>
													</tr>
												}
											</tbody>
										</table>
										@if (guidanceReview.Gaps.Count > 0)
										{
											<h4>Survivors still uncovered</h4>
											<ul class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var gap in guidanceReview.Gaps) { <li>@gap</li> }</ul>
										}
										@if (guidanceReview.Overreach.Count > 0)
										{
											<h4>Asserts implementation detail — will break on refactoring</h4>
											<ul class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var item in guidanceReview.Overreach) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
										}
										@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(guidanceReview.NextStep))
										{
											<h4>Before trusting any of this</h4>
											<p class="rt-reco">@guidanceReview.NextStep</p>
										}
									}
									else if (_session?.RegressionGuidance.Status is "advising" or "reviewing")
									{
										<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Claude is tracing each proposed assertion against the code…</div>
									}
									else
									{
										<div class="rt-placeholder">Claude's assessment of Gemma's proposals will appear here.</div>
									}
									<h4>Read this carefully</h4>
									<ul class="rt-list warn">
										<li>Both model stages are <strong>opinions about tests that do not exist yet</strong>. The mutation score above is executed evidence; nothing below step 4 is.</li>
										<li>The only real proof is to write the proposed tests and re-run the mutation test. If the score does not move, the proposal did not work — whatever either model said about it.</li>
										<li>Claude reviewing Gemma is two models in agreement, not verification. It catches obvious errors; it cannot make an untested claim true.</li>
									</ul>
								</section>
							}
						}
					</section>
					break;
				case 26:
					<section>
						<p class="kicker">REAL DATA, NEVER COMMITTED</p>
						<h2 id="scene-title">The best test data is also the worst leak</h2>
						<p class="rt-intro">A test ticket built from real data reproduces the defect properly — and is a data-exfiltration path if it goes straight to a model. <strong>Not checked in is not the same as not sent.</strong> The gate runs first, the model sees only the scrubbed copy, and the audit record keeps references rather than payloads.</p>

						<section class="rt-box rt-input-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">1</span><div><strong>Ephemeral test ticket</strong><small>real repro data · in-memory only</small></div></header>
							<textarea class="rt-code-input" spellcheck="false" maxlength="12000" @bind="_ephemeralTicket" @bind:event="oninput" disabled="@EphemeralBusy" aria-label="Ephemeral ticket"></textarea>
							<div class="rt-actions">
								<small>@_ephemeralTicket.Length / 12000</small>
								<button class="primary-command compact" type="button" data-auto="s27.run" disabled="@(!_bridgeConnected || _ephemeralTicket.Trim().Length < 20 || EphemeralBusy)" @onclick="RunEphemeral">@(!_bridgeConnected ? "Connect VSIX to run" : EphemeralBusy ? "Running…" : "Gate, then run")</button>
							</div>
							@if (!_bridgeConnected)
							{
								<p class="bridge-required" role="status">Connect the VSIX with the token shown under Local Bridge before running.</p>
							}
						</section>

						@if (_session?.Ephemeral.Gate is { } dataGate)
						{
							<section class="rt-box">
								<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">2</span><div><strong>Pre-flight gate</strong><small>runs before anything leaves the boundary</small></div></header>
								<div class="audit-body">
									<div class="audit-scoreline">
										<span class="ctx-label decision-@dataGate.Decision.ToLowerInvariant().Replace("-", "")">@dataGate.Decision</span>
										<div><strong>@dataGate.TierName</strong><small>@dataGate.Findings.Count finding type(s)</small></div>
										<p>@dataGate.Rationale</p>
									</div>
									@if (_session.Ephemeral.Record is { } record)
									{
										<h4>Ephemeral record</h4>
										<table class="audit-table">
											<tbody>
												<tr><td>Ticket id</td><td>@record.TicketId</td></tr>
												<tr><td>Owner</td><td>@record.Owner</td></tr>
												<tr><td>Storage</td><td>@record.Storage</td></tr>
												<tr><td>Retention</td><td>@record.Ttl</td></tr>
												<tr><td>Logging</td><td>@record.LogPolicy</td></tr>
												<tr><td>Payload digest</td><td><code>@record.PayloadDigest</code></td></tr>
											</tbody>
										</table>
										@if (record.Purged.Count > 0)
										{
											<h4>Removed before the model saw it</h4>
											<ul class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var item in record.Purged) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
										}
									}
								</div>
							</section>

							@if (_session.Ephemeral.Status == "blocked")
							{
								<div class="compare-status failed" role="alert"><strong>Blocked.</strong> Restricted content was found, so nothing was sent to a model. Redaction does not make credentials safe — the owner authorises handling first. This is the gate working, not a failure.</div>
							}
							else
							{
								<div class="rt-flow">
									<section class="rt-box">
										<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">3</span><div><strong>What the model actually received</strong><small>scrubbed copy</small></div></header>
										<pre class="rt-code">@dataGate.Scrubbed</pre>
									</section>
									<section class="rt-box">
										<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">4</span><div><strong>Reproduction plan</strong><small>@(_session.Ephemeral.AgentModel ?? "Gemma")</small></div></header>
										@if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_session.Ephemeral.AgentPlan))
										{
											<div class="rt-story">@_session.Ephemeral.AgentPlan</div>
										}
										else if (EphemeralBusy)
										{
											<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Running the test against the scrubbed ticket…</div>
										}
										else
										{
											<div class="rt-placeholder">The plan will appear here — proving the test still works after scrubbing.</div>
										}
									</section>
								</div>
							}
						}
						@if (_session?.Ephemeral.Status == "failed")
						{
							<div class="compare-status failed" role="alert">@(_session?.Ephemeral.Error ?? "The ephemeral run did not complete.")</div>
						}
					</section>
					break;
				case 27:
					<section>
						<p class="kicker">DISCOVER WIDE, SCOPE NARROW, DESIGN DEEP</p>
						<h2 id="scene-title">Each tier answers a question the tier below it cannot</h2>
						<p class="rt-intro">Cortex maps the whole estate. An <strong>APM ID</strong> bounds what a team owns. A repository's <strong>/okf</strong> bundle is the atomic truth about its own code. The value is not that three tiers exist — it is that each one answers a question the others cannot, and loading them in the wrong order either misses services or buries the model in irrelevant context.</p>

						<div class="rt-actions">
							<small>Deterministic — no model call, works without the bridge.</small>
							<button class="primary-command compact" type="button" data-auto="s28.load" @onclick="RunPortfolio">Load the tiers</button>
						</div>

						@if (_portfolio is { } portfolio)
						{
							<section class="rt-box" data-auto="s28.estate">
								<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">1</span><div><strong>Tier 1 — Cortex global ecosystem</strong><small>@portfolio.Services.Count services · structure, ownership, health</small></div></header>
								<div class="audit-body">
									<table class="audit-table">
										<thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>APM</th><th>Domain</th><th>Client orders</th><th>Health</th><th>Depends on</th></tr></thead>
										<tbody>
											@foreach (var service in portfolio.Services)
											{
												<tr class="@(service.HandlesClientOrders ? "p0-req" : "p0-opt")">
													<td>@service.Name</td>
													<td>@service.AmpId</td>
													<td>@service.Domain</td>
													<td>@(service.HandlesClientOrders ? "yes" : "no")</td>
													<td>@service.Health</td>
													<td>@(service.DependsOn.Count == 0 ? "—" : string.Join(", ", service.DependsOn))</td>
												</tr>
											}
										</tbody>
									</table>
									<p class="ctx-method">Tier 1 answers <em>what exists and what touches what</em>. It does not record regulatory perimeter, asset-class scope, or how a team accepts change — which is exactly why stopping here is dangerous.</p>
								</div>
							</section>

							@if (portfolio.SharedDependencyWarning.Count > 0)
							{
								<section class="rt-box">
									<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">!</span><div><strong>The trap in this estate</strong><small>deterministic — a structural fact, not an opinion</small></div></header>
									<ul class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var line in portfolio.SharedDependencyWarning) { <li>@line</li> }</ul>
								</section>
							}

							<section class="rt-box">
								<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">2</span><div><strong>Tier 2 — APM records</strong><small>team ownership bounds</small></div></header>
								<div class="audit-body">
									<table class="audit-table">
										<thead><tr><th>APM</th><th>Group / team</th><th>Regulatory perimeter</th><th>Asset classes</th><th>Repositories</th></tr></thead>
										<tbody>
											@foreach (var amp in portfolio.Amps)
											{
												var ampId = amp.AmpId;
												<tr class="p0-clickable @(_expandedAmp == ampId ? "curve-plateau" : null)" data-auto="s28.amp-@ampId" @onclick="() => ToggleAmp(ampId)">
													<td>@amp.AmpId</td>
													<td>@amp.Name<br /><small>@amp.Team</small></td>
													<td>@amp.RegulatoryPerimeter</td>
													<td>@string.Join(", ", amp.AssetClasses)</td>
													<td>@(amp.Repositories.Count == 0 ? "—" : string.Join(", ", amp.Repositories))</td>
												</tr>
												@if (_expandedAmp == ampId)
												{
													<tr><td colspan="5"><em>Scope note:</em> @amp.ScopeNote</td></tr>
												}
											}
										</tbody>
									</table>
									<p class="ctx-method">Tier 2 answers <em>who owns this and what are they allowed to change</em>. Select a row for its scope note.</p>
								</div>
							</section>

							<section class="rt-box">
								<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">3</span><div><strong>Tier 3 — repository /okf bundles</strong><small>atomic truth, read from disk</small></div></header>
								<div class="repo-grid">
									@foreach (var repo in portfolio.Repositories)
									{
										<article class="repo-card">
											<h3>@repo.Name</h3>
											<p class="repo-asset">@repo.AmpId · @repo.Service</p>
											<p class="repo-diverge">@(repo.Available ? string.Join(", ", repo.OkfTypes) : "OKF bundle not found on disk")</p>
											<p class="repo-stats">@repo.OkfDocuments OKF documents · @repo.CodeFiles source files</p>
										</article>
									}
								</div>
								<p class="ctx-method">@portfolio.CorpusStatus Tier 3 answers <em>how this repository actually works</em> — stage sequence, contracts, documented behaviour. It cannot tell you which repositories to open.</p>
							</section>

							<section class="rt-box">
								<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">4</span><div><strong>The design brief</strong><small>FRAUD-2140 · what the estate is being asked to absorb</small></div></header>
								<pre class="rt-code">@PortfolioTierSamples.DesignBrief</pre>
							</section>

							<section class="rt-box">
								<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">5</span><div><strong>Claude Opus 4.8 walks the funnel</strong><small>one tier per stage, deliberately</small></div></header>
								<div class="audit-body">
									<div class="know-grid">
										<div class="know-col own"><p class="eyebrow">TIER 1 → DISCOVER</p><ul><li>@portfolio.Cost.Tier1Tokens.ToString("N0") tokens. Which services could this brief touch?</li></ul></div>
										<div class="know-col learned"><p class="eyebrow">TIER 2 → SCOPE</p><ul><li>@portfolio.Cost.Tier2Tokens.ToString("N0") tokens. Which of those are genuinely in scope, and why?</li></ul></div>
										<div class="know-col unverified"><p class="eyebrow">TIER 3 → DESIGN</p><ul><li>@portfolio.Cost.Tier3TokensInScope.ToString("N0") tokens for the in-scope repos only.</li></ul></div>
									</div>
									<p class="rt-reco">Loading every repository's Tier 3 up front would cost <strong>@portfolio.Cost.Tier3TokensEverything.ToString("N0")</strong> tokens instead of @portfolio.Cost.Tier3TokensInScope.ToString("N0") — and would hand the model the crypto desk's context while asking it to exclude the crypto desk. The funnel is a correctness control before it is a cost control.</p>
									<div class="rt-actions">
										<small>Each stage receives only its own tier. @(portfolio.Cost.Exact ? "Token counts are exact." : "Token counts are estimated.")</small>
										<button class="primary-command compact" type="button" data-auto="s28.tiers" disabled="@(!_bridgeConnected || TierBusy)" @onclick="RunPortfolioTiers">@TierButtonText</button>
									</div>
									@if (!_bridgeConnected)
									{
										<p class="bridge-required" role="status">Connect the VSIX with the token shown under Local Bridge before running.</p>
									}
									@if (_session?.PortfolioTiers.Error is { } tierError)
									{
										<div class="compare-status failed" role="alert">@tierError</div>
									}
								</div>
							</section>

							@if (_session?.PortfolioTiers.Discovery is { } discovery)
							{
								<section class="rt-box">
									<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">5a</span><div><strong>Tier 1 result — candidates</strong><small>@discovery.Candidates.Count found</small></div></header>
									<div class="audit-body">
										<p class="rt-reco">@discovery.Summary</p>
										<table class="audit-table">
											<thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>APM</th><th>Why it is a candidate</th></tr></thead>
											<tbody>
												@foreach (var candidate in discovery.Candidates)
												{
													<tr><td>@candidate.Service</td><td>@candidate.AmpId</td><td>@candidate.Why</td></tr>
												}
											</tbody>
										</table>
										@if (discovery.CannotDetermineYet.Count > 0)
										{
											<h4>What Tier 1 could not settle</h4>
											<ul class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var item in discovery.CannotDetermineYet) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
										}
									</div>
								</section>
							}
							else if (_session?.PortfolioTiers.Status == "tier1")
							{
								<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Claude is reading the Cortex ecosystem map…</div>
							}

							@if (_session?.PortfolioTiers.Scoping is { } scoping)
							{
								<section class="rt-box">
									<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">5b</span><div><strong>Tier 2 result — scope</strong><small>@scoping.Decisions.Count(item => item.InScope) in scope</small></div></header>
									<div class="audit-body">
										<p class="rt-reco">@scoping.Summary</p>
										<table class="audit-table">
											<thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Decision</th><th>Reason</th><th>Tier 2 evidence</th></tr></thead>
											<tbody>
												@foreach (var scopeRow in scoping.Decisions)
												{
													<tr class="@(scopeRow.InScope ? "p0-opt" : "p0-req")">
														<td>@scopeRow.Service</td>
														<td>@(scopeRow.InScope ? "IN SCOPE" : "excluded")</td>
														<td>@scopeRow.Reason</td>
														<td>@scopeRow.Evidence</td>
													</tr>
												}
											</tbody>
										</table>
										@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(scoping.SharedLibraryVerdict))
										{
											<h4>Ruling on the shared library</h4>
											<p class="rt-reco">@scoping.SharedLibraryVerdict</p>
										}
									</div>
								</section>
							}
							else if (_session?.PortfolioTiers.Status == "tier2")
							{
								<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Claude is applying the APM ownership bounds…</div>
							}

							@if (_session?.PortfolioTiers.Designs.Count > 0)
							{
								@foreach (var tierDesign in _session.PortfolioTiers.Designs)
								{
									<section class="rt-box">
										<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">5c</span><div><strong>Tier 3 design — @tierDesign.Service</strong><small>@tierDesign.Repository · from its own /okf bundle</small></div></header>
										<div class="audit-body">
											<p class="rt-reco">@tierDesign.Summary</p>
											@if (tierDesign.Changes.Count > 0)
											{
												<table class="audit-table">
													<thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Change</th><th>Justified by</th></tr></thead>
													<tbody>
														@foreach (var edit in tierDesign.Changes)
														{
															<tr><td><code>@edit.File</code></td><td>@edit.Change</td><td>@edit.Justification</td></tr>
														}
													</tbody>
												</table>
											}
											@if (tierDesign.Unchanged.Count > 0)
											{
												<h4>Must stay unchanged</h4>
												<ul class="rt-list good">@foreach (var item in tierDesign.Unchanged) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
											}
											@if (tierDesign.Risks.Count > 0)
											{
												<h4>Risks</h4>
												<ul class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var item in tierDesign.Risks) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
											}
											@if (tierDesign.OpenQuestions.Count > 0)
											{
												<h4>Open questions</h4>
												<ul class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var item in tierDesign.OpenQuestions) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
											}
										</div>
									</section>
								}
							}
							else if (_session?.PortfolioTiers.Status == "tier3")
							{
								<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Claude is designing the change in each in-scope repository…</div>
							}

							<section class="rt-qa">
								<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">·</span><div><strong>What this demonstrates</strong><small>and what it does not</small></div></header>
								<ul class="rt-list good">
									<li><strong>Tier 1 alone over-scopes.</strong> Three services handle client orders and all three share one library. The cheapest-looking fix is to change the shared library, which would impose broker-dealer fraud screening on a desk in a different regulatory perimeter.</li>
									<li><strong>Tier 2 is what makes the exclusion defensible.</strong> "It sounds like crypto" is not evidence. APM-1187's asset classes and MSB perimeter are.</li>
									<li><strong>Tier 3 is the only tier that can name a file.</strong> The stage sequence and the <code>IOrderStage</code> contract come from each repository's own bundle, not from the catalogue.</li>
								</ul>
								<ul class="rt-list warn">
									<li>Tier 1 and Tier 2 here are an authored fixture modelled on Cortex and APM records. Tier 3 is real: the OKF bundles are read from the repositories on disk.</li>
									<li>The funnel is only as good as the tier metadata. If APM-1187 had not recorded its perimeter, no amount of model capability would have justified the exclusion — it would have been a guess that happened to be right.</li>
									<li>Claude's scoping and design are a model's judgement. The structure, the token costs and the shared-dependency warning are deterministic.</li>
								</ul>
							</section>
						}
					</section>
					break;
				case 28:
					<section>
						<p class="kicker">THREE REAL SERVICES, ONE SHARED SPINE</p>
						<h2 id="scene-title">Find the duplication by meaning, then let the right model do each job</h2>
						<p class="rt-intro">Three production broker-dealer services are read from disk. They share an identical framework spine and diverge completely in their trading logic. <strong>embeddinggemma</strong> finds the duplication by meaning, <strong>Claude Opus 5</strong> designs the consolidation, and <strong>Gemma 4</strong> writes the code from that design — the expensive model is billed for judgement, not for typing.</p>

						<section class="rt-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">1</span><div><strong>The corpus</strong><small>real repositories, not a fixture</small></div></header>
							<div class="repo-grid">
								@foreach (var repo in TradingCorpus.Repos)
								{
									var loaded = _commonCode?.Repos.FirstOrDefault(item => item.Name == repo.Name);
									<article class="repo-card">
										<h3>@repo.Name</h3>
										<p class="repo-asset">@repo.AssetClass</p>
										<p class="repo-diverge">@repo.Divergence</p>
										<dl class="verdict-meta"><dt>OKF quality</dt><dd>@repo.OkfQuality</dd></dl>
										@if (loaded is not null)
										{
											<p class="repo-stats">@loaded.Files files · @loaded.Lines lines · @loaded.NonFunctionalFiles framework / @loaded.FunctionalFiles trading</p>
										}
									</article>
								}
							</div>
							<div class="rt-actions">
								<small>Deterministic — embeddings only, no bridge needed.</small>
								<button class="primary-command compact" type="button" data-auto="s29.analyse" disabled="@_commonCodeRunning" @onclick="RunCommonCode">@(_commonCodeRunning ? "Embedding…" : "Run the audit")</button>
							</div>
						</section>

						@if (_commonCode is { } codeAudit)
						{
							<span data-auto="s29.clusters" hidden></span>
							@if (!codeAudit.CorpusAvailable)
							{
								<div class="rt-error" role="alert">@codeAudit.CorpusStatus</div>
							}
							else
							{
								<section class="rt-box">
									<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">2</span><div><strong>Did it actually separate them?</strong><small>scored against the source tree, not asserted</small></div></header>
									<div class="audit-body">
										<div class="know-grid">
											<div class="know-col learned"><p class="eyebrow">KNOWN DUPLICATES</p><ul><li>mean @codeAudit.Separation.DuplicateMean.ToString("0.000"), weakest @codeAudit.Separation.DuplicateMin.ToString("0.000")</li></ul></div>
											<div class="know-col unverified"><p class="eyebrow">EVERYTHING ELSE</p><ul><li>mean @codeAudit.Separation.UnrelatedMean.ToString("0.000"), strongest @codeAudit.Separation.UnrelatedMax.ToString("0.000")</li></ul></div>
											<div class="know-col own"><p class="eyebrow">MARGIN</p><ul><li>@codeAudit.Separation.Margin.ToString("0.000") — @codeAudit.Separation.NearestNeighbourHits/@codeAudit.Separation.NearestNeighbourTotal framework files whose nearest cross-repo neighbour is the same class</li></ul></div>
										</div>
										<p class="ctx-method">@codeAudit.CorpusStatus Method: @(codeAudit.UsedEmbeddings ? "embeddinggemma-300m int8, windowed mean-pooling over whole files" : "token-overlap fallback") at cosine ≥ @codeAudit.Threshold.ToString("0.000"). @(codeAudit.Separation.Margin > 0 ? $"The two populations do not overlap, but the margin is only {codeAudit.Separation.Margin:0.000} wide — a single threshold works here and would not survive a noisier estate." : "The populations overlap: no single threshold separates them cleanly, so treat the clusters as candidates for review rather than findings.")</p>
									</div>
								</section>

								<section class="rt-box">
									<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">3</span><div><strong>The prize</strong><small>@codeAudit.DuplicatedClusters duplicated cluster(s) across @codeAudit.UnitCount files</small></div></header>
									<div class="audit-body">
										<div class="know-grid">
											<div class="know-col learned"><p class="eyebrow">NON-FUNCTIONAL DUPLICATION</p><ul><li>@codeAudit.NonFunctionalPrize lines — framework code with one correct answer. Start here.</li></ul></div>
											<div class="know-col unverified"><p class="eyebrow">FUNCTIONAL DUPLICATION</p><ul><li>@(codeAudit.FunctionalPrize == 0 ? "None found. The trading logic genuinely diverges by asset class — which is also evidence the audit is not simply clustering everything that looks like C#." : $"{codeAudit.FunctionalPrize} lines — business rules encoded more than once. Higher prize, higher risk.")</li></ul></div>
										</div>
										<table class="audit-table">
											<thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Members</th><th>Repos</th><th>Duplicate lines</th><th>Recommendation</th></tr></thead>
											<tbody>
												@foreach (var cluster in codeAudit.Clusters.Where(cluster => cluster.IsDuplication))
												{
													<tr class="p0-req">
														<td>@cluster.Kind</td>
														<td>@string.Join(", ", cluster.Members.Select(member => $"{member.Repo}/{member.Name}"))</td>
														<td>@cluster.Repos.Count</td>
														<td>@cluster.DuplicateLines</td>
														<td>@cluster.Recommendation</td>
													</tr>
												}
											</tbody>
										</table>
										<ol class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var step in codeAudit.Strategy) { <li>@step</li> }</ol>
									</div>
								</section>

								@if (codeAudit.TopPairs.Count > 0)
								{
									<section class="rt-box">
										<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">4</span><div><strong>How the threshold was chosen</strong><small>measured, not guessed</small></div></header>
										<div class="audit-body">
											<table class="audit-table">
												<thead><tr><th>Similarity</th><th>Pair</th><th>Cross-repo</th><th>Clustered</th></tr></thead>
												<tbody>
													@foreach (var pair in codeAudit.TopPairs)
													{
														<tr class="@(pair.Similarity >= codeAudit.Threshold ? "p0-req" : "p0-opt")">
															<td>@pair.Similarity.ToString("0.000")</td>
															<td>@pair.Left ~ @pair.Right</td>
															<td>@(pair.CrossRepo ? "yes" : "no")</td>
															<td>@(pair.Similarity >= codeAudit.Threshold ? "yes" : "below threshold")</td>
														</tr>
													}
												</tbody>
											</table>
											<p class="ctx-method">These are the pairs either side of the cut, not the obvious top of the list. The threshold sits in the measured gap between the weakest true duplicate and the strongest unrelated pair — here that gap is narrow, and the nearest miss is a genuine near-relative rather than noise. Re-measure with <code>--calibrate-corpus</code> before pointing this at a different estate.</p>
										</div>
									</section>
								}

								<section class="rt-box">
									<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">5</span><div><strong>Claude Opus 5 designs the consolidation</strong><small>judgement, not typing</small></div></header>
									<div class="rt-actions">
										<small>Claude sees the audit; the implementation spec it writes is the only thing Gemma will see.</small>
										<button class="primary-command compact" type="button" data-auto="s29.consolidate" disabled="@(!_bridgeConnected || codeAudit.DuplicatedClusters == 0 || ConsolidationBusy)" @onclick="RunConsolidation">@ConsolidationButtonText</button>
									</div>
									@if (!_bridgeConnected)
									{
										<p class="bridge-required" role="status">Connect the VSIX with the token shown under Local Bridge before running.</p>
									}
									@if (_session?.Consolidation.Error is { } consolidationError)
									{
										<div class="rt-error" role="alert">@consolidationError</div>
									}
									@if (_session?.Consolidation.Design is { } sharedDesign)
									{
										<div class="audit-body">
											<div class="coach-label">Designed by @_session.Consolidation.DesignModel</div>
											<h4>@sharedDesign.LibraryName</h4>
											<p class="rt-reco">@sharedDesign.Summary</p>
											@if (sharedDesign.Modules.Count > 0)
											{
												<table class="audit-table">
													<thead><tr><th>Module</th><th>Responsibility</th><th>Public API</th><th>Replaces</th></tr></thead>
													<tbody>
														@foreach (var module in sharedDesign.Modules)
														{
															<tr><td>@module.Name</td><td>@module.Responsibility</td><td><code>@module.PublicApi</code></td><td>@string.Join(", ", module.Replaces)</td></tr>
														}
													</tbody>
												</table>
											}
											@if (sharedDesign.MigrationSteps.Count > 0)
											{
												<h4>Migration</h4><ol class="rt-list good">@foreach (var step in sharedDesign.MigrationSteps) { <li>@step</li> }</ol>
											}
											@if (sharedDesign.Risks.Count > 0)
											{
												<h4>Risks</h4><ul class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var risk in sharedDesign.Risks) { <li>@risk</li> }</ul>
											}
											@if (sharedDesign.OutOfScope.Count > 0)
											{
												<h4>Deliberately not consolidated</h4><ul class="rt-list">@foreach (var item in sharedDesign.OutOfScope) { <li>@item</li> }</ul>
											}
											<h4>Implementation spec handed to Gemma</h4>
											<pre class="rt-code">@sharedDesign.ImplementationSpec</pre>
										</div>
									}
									else if (_session?.Consolidation.Status == "designing")
									{
										<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Claude is designing the shared library from the audit…</div>
									}
									else
									{
										<div class="rt-placeholder">Claude's consolidation design will appear here.</div>
									}
								</section>

								<section class="rt-box">
									<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">6</span><div><strong>Gemma 4 implements the design</strong><small>one task per module, spec in, code out — no repository access</small></div></header>
									@if (_session?.Consolidation.Build is { } build)
									{
										<div class="audit-body">
											<div class="coach-label">@(build.ModulesCompleted)/@(build.ModulesTotal) modules · implemented by @(_session.Consolidation.BuildModel ?? "Gemma") from the spec alone — it never saw the three repositories.</div>
											@if (build.FailedModules.Count > 0)
											{
												<h4>Modules that failed</h4><ul class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var failure in build.FailedModules) { <li>@failure</li> }</ul>
											}
											@if (build.Assumptions.Count > 0)
											{
												<h4>Gaps the spec left open</h4><ul class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var assumption in build.Assumptions) { <li>@assumption</li> }</ul>
											}
											@foreach (var file in build.Files)
											{
												<h4>@file.Path</h4>
												<p class="repo-diverge">@file.Purpose</p>
												<pre class="rt-code">@file.Source</pre>
											}
											@if (build.ModulesCompleted < build.ModulesTotal)
											{
												<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Building module @(build.ModulesCompleted + 1) of @build.ModulesTotal…</div>
											}
										</div>
									}
									else if (_session?.Consolidation.Status is "designing" or "building")
									{
										<div class="rt-pending"><span></span>Waiting for the design before the modules can be built…</div>
									}
									else
									{
										<div class="rt-placeholder">Gemma's implementation will appear here.</div>
									}
								</section>

								@if (_session?.Consolidation.Tokens is { } spend)
								{
									<section class="rt-qa">
										<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">!</span><div><strong>Where the tokens went</strong><small>@(spend.Exact ? "exact Gemma tokenizer counts" : "estimated")</small></div></header>
										<table class="audit-table">
											<thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Model</th><th>Prompt tokens</th><th>Output tokens</th><th>What it bought</th></tr></thead>
											<tbody>
												<tr><td>Design</td><td>@(_session.Consolidation.DesignModel ?? "Claude Opus 5")</td><td>@spend.DesignPromptTokens.ToString("N0")</td><td>@spend.DesignOutputTokens.ToString("N0")</td><td>Boundaries, migration sequence, risk — the part that needs judgement.</td></tr>
												<tr><td>Build</td><td>@(_session.Consolidation.BuildModel ?? "Gemma 4")</td><td>@spend.BuildPromptTokens.ToString("N0")</td><td>@spend.BuildOutputTokens.ToString("N0")</td><td>Volume code from a closed specification — mechanical.</td></tr>
											</tbody>
										</table>
										<ul class="rt-list good">
											<li>The frontier model never received the corpus. Sending all @spend.CorpusTokens.ToString("N0") tokens of source to Claude would have cost roughly @((spend.CorpusTokens / (double)Math.Max(spend.DesignPromptTokens, 1)).ToString("0.0"))× the design prompt, before it wrote a line.</li>
											<li>@(spend.BuildOutputTokens > spend.DesignOutputTokens ? "Most of the generated volume came from the cheaper model, which is the intended split." : "The design was larger than the implementation here — on a bigger consolidation the ratio inverts.")</li>
											<li>This only holds if the spec is genuinely self-contained. If Gemma has to guess, the retry cost lands back on the expensive model — see the token economics scene for cost per successful outcome.</li>
										</ul>
									</section>
								}
							}
						}
					</section>
					break;
				case 29:
					<section>
						<p class="kicker">FREE IS THE WRONG WORD</p>
						<h2 id="scene-title">Budget in cost per outcome, not cost per token</h2>
						<p class="rt-intro">An open-weight model has <strong>no per-token vendor invoice</strong> — it does not have zero cost. And a model that fails a third of the time is billed for every failure. The only unit that survives contact with Finance is <strong>cost per successful outcome</strong>.</p>

						<div class="rt-actions">
							<small>Deterministic — illustrative rates, no model call.</small>
							<button class="primary-command compact" type="button" data-auto="s30.run" @onclick="RunEconomics">Compute the economics</button>
						</div>

						@if (_economics is { } econ)
						{
							<section class="rt-box" data-auto="s30.result">
								<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">1</span><div><strong>The escalation ladder</strong><small>@econ.PromptTokens.ToString("N0") prompt + @econ.OutputTokens.ToString("N0") output tokens per attempt</small></div></header>
								<div class="audit-body">
									<table class="audit-table">
										<thead><tr><th>Rung</th><th>Model</th><th>Billing</th><th>Success</th><th>Cost / attempt</th><th>Attempts / success</th><th>Cost / success</th></tr></thead>
										<tbody>
											@foreach (var row in econ.Rows)
											{
												<tr class="@(row.Rung == econ.CheapestPerSuccess ? "econ-best" : null)">
													<td>@row.Rung</td>
													<td>@row.Model</td>
													<td>@row.Kind</td>
													<td>@row.SuccessPercent%</td>
													<td>@row.CostPerAttempt.ToString("C4")</td>
													<td>@row.AttemptsPerSuccess</td>
													<td><strong>@row.CostPerSuccess.ToString("C4")</strong></td>
												</tr>
											}
										</tbody>
									</table>
									<ul class="rt-list good">@foreach (var row in econ.Rows) { <li><strong>@row.Model:</strong> @row.Note</li> }</ul>
								</div>
							</section>

							@if (econ.RateCardMisleads)
							{
								<div class="compare-status" role="status"><strong>The rate card would pick the wrong model.</strong> Cheapest per attempt is <em>@econ.CheapestPerAttempt</em>; cheapest per success is <em>@econ.CheapestPerSuccess</em>. Routing on price alone buys more retries, not more outcomes.</div>
							}

							<section class="rt-qa">
								<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">2</span><div><strong>Routing policy</strong><small>what to tell the teams</small></div></header>
								<ol class="rt-list warn">@foreach (var line in econ.Policy) { <li>@line</li> }</ol>
							</section>
						}
					</section>
					break;
				case 30:
					<section>
						<p class="kicker">A LIBRARY THAT SCALES WHAT WORKS</p>
						<h2 id="scene-title">Contributions are admitted on evidence, then run</h2>
						<p class="rt-intro">A shared prompt library scales whatever you put in it — including the mistakes. So there is an <strong>entry gate</strong> rather than an upload button. But complete paperwork does not prove a prompt works, so an admitted contribution is then <strong>executed</strong> against a real class, and a second model judges what the prompt caused.</p>

						<section class="rt-box rt-input-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">1</span><div><strong>Contribute a pattern</strong><small>pre-filled with a working example — edit any field to see the gate react</small></div></header>
							<div class="p0-form">
								<label>Title<input type="text" @bind="_submission.Title" /></label>
								<label>Problem it solves<input type="text" @bind="_submission.Problem" /></label>
								<label>Evidence of outcome (include a number)<input type="text" @bind="_submission.Evidence" /></label>
								<label>Context it depends on<input type="text" @bind="_submission.ContextNeeded" /></label>
								<label>Known failure modes<input type="text" @bind="_submission.FailureModes" /></label>
							</div>
							<label class="p0-prompt-label">The prompt itself — this is the artefact being shared, and the instruction Gemma will receive</label>
