								<li>One execution against one class is a demonstration, not the evidence the gate asks for. The Evidence field should carry a measured rate across many runs — this scene shows you how one of those runs is produced.</li>
								<li>Claude reviewing Gemma is a second opinion, not verification. It cannot tell you the prompt generalises.</li>
								<li>The library admits on documentation quality. Nothing here stops a well-documented prompt that is simply wrong — which is why contributions carry failure modes and get re-reviewed.</li>
							</ul>
						</section>
					</section>
					break;
				case 31:
					<section>
						<p class="kicker">PLAN BEFORE CODE</p>
						<h2 id="scene-title">A summary leadership reads, a diagram engineers check</h2>
						<p class="rt-intro">Demanding a plan with an executive summary and a diagram is a <strong>graded skill</strong>, not a nicety. The hardest check is the last one: producing an implementation before the plan is reviewed is exactly the habit this gate exists to break.</p>

