				case 33:
					<section>
						<p class="kicker">GROUND THE CHEAP MODEL, THEN DELEGATE TO IT</p>
						<h2 id="scene-title">Making Gemma 4 a crypto SME</h2>
						<p class="rt-intro">Claude Opus 5 is a strong generalist. On a domain with exact header names, exact defaults and exact error semantics, "strong generalist" is not the same as "will get it right". Here Claude answers <strong>unaided</strong> first, then consults a <strong>grounded Gemma 4</strong> as a subagent, then designs. The improvement is measured against verified facts — not asserted.</p>

						<section class="rt-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">1</span><div><strong>The requirement</strong><small>CRY-4417 · a real design task, not a quiz</small></div></header>
							<pre class="rt-code">@CryptoSmeCorpus.Jira</pre>
						</section>

						<section class="rt-box">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">2</span><div><strong>What Gemma is grounded on</strong><small>three layers · @CryptoSmeCorpus.Facts.Count verified facts</small></div></header>
							<div class="audit-body">
								<div class="know-grid">
									<div class="know-col own"><p class="eyebrow">LAYER 1 · UNIFIED</p><ul><li>CCXT — one API across 100+ venues, CCXT Pro for WebSocket streaming. Keeps venue two from being a rewrite.</li></ul></div>
									<div class="know-col learned"><p class="eyebrow">LAYER 2 · VENUE MECHANICS</p><ul><li>Binance spot: weight-based rate limiting, timing and signature rules, symbol filters, unknown-outcome handling.</li></ul></div>
									<div class="know-col unverified"><p class="eyebrow">LAYER 3 · FIRM RULES</p><ul><li>Decimal-only arithmetic, per-service credentials, dedicated egress, firm-generated client order ids. Synthetic here; real policy in production.</li></ul></div>
								</div>
								<h4>Sources the pack was built from</h4>
								<ul class="rt-list good">@foreach (var source in CryptoSmeCorpus.Sources) { <li><a href="@source.Url" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@source.Label</a></li> }</ul>
								<p class="ctx-method">Layers 1 and 2 were transcribed from these pages and each fact is cited in the pack. Layer 3 is synthetic and labelled as such. Today this is a curated pack; the stated intent is that Gemma later runs internally with no per-token vendor cost, carrying both the industry rules and the firm's own.</p>
							</div>
						</section>

						<div class="rt-actions">
							<small>Three stages: Claude unaided, Gemma grounded, Claude designs.</small>
							<button class="primary-command compact" type="button" data-auto="s34.run" disabled="@(!_bridgeConnected || SmeBusy)" @onclick="RunCryptoSme">@SmeButtonText</button>
