												</tr>
											}
										</tbody>
									</table>
								}
							</div>
						</section>

						<section class="rt-box" data-auto="fx.instruction">
							<header class="rt-head"><span class="rt-step">3</span><div><strong>The Focus/Ignore instruction, exactly as it will be sent</strong><small>@(fx?.InstructionTokens > 0 ? $"{fx.InstructionTokens:N0} tokens · written by code from the table above" : "appears after Step 2")</small></div></header>
							<div class="audit-body">
								<p>
									<strong>Why it is built this way.</strong> The instruction names section numbers and titles only. It does not
									summarise the crypto content, because a summary would be a model's opinion smuggled into the prompt; it does
									not say <em>why</em> a section is crypto, because the classifier does not know why. It also names the sections
									that <em>look</em> like crypto but are referenced by a bond section, so the traps are protected the same way
									removal protected them. Everything else it tells the model to read in full.
								</p>
								@if (fx?.Instruction is { } fxInstruction)
