													<td>@arm.PromptTokens.ToString("N0")</td>
													<td>@Delta(fxA?.PromptTokens, arm.PromptTokens, arm.Arm == "A")</td>
													<td>@(arm.Status == "completed" ? arm.OutputTokens.ToString("N0") : "—")</td>
													<td>@(arm.Status == "completed" && fxA?.Status == "completed" ? Delta(fxA.OutputTokens, arm.OutputTokens, arm.Arm == "A") : "—")</td>
													<td>@(arm.Status == "completed" ? ArmCost(arm).ToString("$0.0000") : "—")</td>
													<td>@(arm.Status == "completed" && fxA?.Status == "completed" ? CostDelta(fxA, arm) : "—")</td>
													<td>@(arm.Status == "completed" ? (arm.Compiled ? "yes" : "NO") : "—")</td>
													<td>@(arm.Status == "completed" && arm.Compiled ? $"{arm.Passed} / {ClassifyContextSamples.TestVectors.Length}" : "—")</td>
													<td>@(arm.Status == "completed" ? (arm.LeakedTerms.Count == 0 ? "none" : string.Join(", ", arm.LeakedTerms)) : "—")</td>
													<td>@(arm.Status == "pending" ? "queued — waiting for the bridge" : arm.Status == "running" ? "Claude is writing the code…" : arm.Status == "failed" ? arm.Error : arm.ModelUsed)</td>
												</tr>
											}
										</tbody>
									</table>
									<p class="rt-note">
										<strong>How to read it.</strong> If I matches B on cases and beats A on output tokens, naming the noise is worth
										its small input cost. If I and A are the same, the instruction bought nothing and removal (B) is the only lever.
										If I fails a case A passed, the instruction confused the model &mdash; a result worth knowing before anyone
										puts &ldquo;ignore the following&rdquo; into a production prompt.
										<em>Illustrative cost</em> weights output tokens at @TokenEconomicsService.VendorOutputPerMillion.ToString("$0")/M against input at
										@TokenEconomicsService.VendorInputPerMillion.ToString("$0")/M &mdash; the same illustrative rates as the token-economics scene, not a
										contract price. At that ratio, one output token saved is worth five input tokens spent, which is why an instruction that
										makes the prompt <em>longer</em> can still make the call <em>cheaper</em>.
									</p>

									@foreach (var arm in fx.Arms.Where(a => a.Status == "completed"))
